Design a pulse-width modulation (PWM) generator. The module takes a clock input and a 7-bit duty cycle value to control the output signal. The output will be HIGH for a duration proportional to the duty cycle and LOW otherwise, cycling at a frequency determined by the clock. The count variable tracks the current state of the PWM cycle, resetting every 100 clock cycles, which sets the PWM period.
