Design a bidirectional buffer with tri-state output functionality for two signals. When the control signal T is asserted, both outputs O and OB go into a high-impedance state (Z), effectively disconnecting them from the inputs. When T is low, output O reflects the input I, while output OB provides the inverted value of I. This module can be used for driving signals in scenarios where buffer isolation and signal inversion are required.
